"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[548],{771(e,o,t){t.r(o),t.d(o,{_pageData:()=>a,default:()=>r});var s=t(641);const a=JSON.parse('{"path":"/bagisto-connector/logs-and-history.html","title":"Logs & History","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"next":"/bagisto-connector/troubleshooting-faq.md"},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"bagisto-connector/logs-and-history.md"}'),n={name:"logs-and-history.md"},r=(0,t(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,o,t,a,n,r){return(0,s.uX)(),(0,s.CE)("div",null,[...o[0]||(o[0]=[(0,s.Fv)('<h1 id="logs-history" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#logs-history"><span>Logs &amp; History</span></a></h1><p>Monitoring the synchronization process is crucial for maintaining data integrity between WooCommerce and Bagisto. The plugin provides a comprehensive logging system to track all API activities, successes, and errors.</p><p>Navigate to <strong>WC to Bagisto</strong> &gt; <strong>Logs</strong> to view the sync history.</p><p><img src="/bagisto-connector/images/bagisto-connector/logs.png" alt="Logs"></p><hr><h2 id="understanding-the-logs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#understanding-the-logs"><span>Understanding the Logs</span></a></h2><p>The log table displays all recorded events related to the connector.</p><ul><li><strong>Date &amp; Time:</strong> The exact timestamp when the event occurred.</li><li><strong>Entity Type:</strong> The type of data being processed (e.g., Product, Category, Order, Customer).</li><li><strong>Action:</strong> The operation performed (e.g., Create, Update, Delete).</li><li><strong>Status:</strong> The result of the operation: <ul><li><span style="color:green;"><strong>Success:</strong></span> The record was successfully synced to Bagisto.</li><li><span style="color:red;"><strong>Error:</strong></span> The synchronization failed.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Message / Details:</strong> A detailed response from the Bagisto API or an internal error message. If an error occurs, this column will provide clues as to why (e.g., &quot;Missing API token&quot;, &quot;SKU already exists&quot;).</li></ul><hr><h2 id="log-management" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#log-management"><span>Log Management</span></a></h2><h3 id="filtering-logs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#filtering-logs"><span>Filtering Logs</span></a></h3><p>You can filter the log entries by <strong>Entity Type</strong> or <strong>Status</strong> to quickly find specific events, such as checking for all failed product syncs.</p><h3 id="clearing-logs" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#clearing-logs"><span>Clearing Logs</span></a></h3><p>Logs can accumulate over time and consume database space.</p><ul><li><strong>Manual Deletion:</strong> You can select specific log entries and delete them using the bulk actions dropdown.</li><li><strong>Automatic Cleanup:</strong> The plugin includes an automated daily cron event (<code>wkwctobag_daily_log_cleanup_event</code>) that automatically clears expired or older logs to keep your database optimized.</li></ul><blockquote><p>[!TIP] If a synchronization fails, the log message is your best resource for troubleshooting. Check the message carefully to see if the issue is related to missing data, incorrect API credentials, or network errors.</p></blockquote>',16)])])}]])}}]);